  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGOKLDimension.standardized_rgo_unique_prox_and_kl_le_dimension",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/SmoothedPicardHMC/StandardizedRGOKLDimension.lean",
    "statement": "\n    {E S : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    [MeasurableSpace S] {V : E → ℝ} {κ : ℝ}\n    (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E, κ⁻¹*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ∧\n      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ≤ ‖v‖^2)\n    {eta : S → ℝ} {y : S → E} (heta : Measurable eta) (hy : Measurable y)\n    (hpos : ∀ s, 0 < eta s) :\n    ∃ p : S → E, Measurable p ∧\n      (∀ s, p s+eta s • gradient V (p s)=y s) ∧\n      (∀ s z, z+eta s • gradient V z=y s → z=p s) ∧\n      let rho := fun s u => V (p s+Real.sqrt (eta s) • u)-V (p s)-\n        Real.sqrt (eta s)*inner ℝ (gradient V (p s)) u\n      let mu := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n      let R := fun s => mu.tilted (fun x => -‖x-y s‖^2/(2*eta s))\n      let r := fun s => (R s).map (fun x => (Real.sqrt (eta s))⁻¹ • (x-p s))\n      let gamma := stdGaussian E\n      ∀ s, IsProbabilityMeasure (r s) ∧ r s ≪ gamma ∧\n        _root_.InformationTheory.klDiv (r s) gamma ≠ ⊤ ∧\n        MemLp (gradient (rho s)) 2 (r s) ∧\n        (_root_.InformationTheory.klDiv (r s) gamma).toReal ≤\n          (eta s)^2*(Module.finrank ℝ E : ℝ)/2",
    "statement_sha256": "2886123363f66b324011cc751d2c1d777646faf9788f9ffdb4fa9374fc66879b",
    "compiled": true
  },
  "blind_reconstruction": {
    "text": "Let E be any complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space, equipped with its norm and Borel measurable structure, and let S be any measurable space. Write d = dim_R(E), a finite natural number, allowing d = 0. Let V : E -> R and kappa : R satisfy kappa >= 1, V be globally twice continuously Frechet differentiable, and, for every x,v in E,\n    kappa^(-1) ||v||^2 <= D^2 V(x)[v,v] <= ||v||^2.\nLet eta : S -> R and y : S -> E be measurable, with eta(s) > 0 for every s in S. There is no upper bound required on eta.\nThen there exists a measurable p : S -> E such that, for every s in S,\n    p(s) + eta(s) grad V(p(s)) = y(s),\nand, for every z in E,\n    z + eta(s) grad V(z) = y(s) implies z = p(s).\nFor this same p define, for s in S and u in E,\n    rho_s(u) = V(p(s) + sqrt(eta(s)) u) - V(p(s))\n               - sqrt(eta(s)) <grad V(p(s)),u>.\nLet vol_E be canonical volume measure, let mu be its normalized exponential tilt by -V, let R_s be the normalized exponential tilt of mu by x |-> -||x-y(s)||^2/(2 eta(s)), and let r_s be the pushforward of R_s under x |-> (sqrt(eta(s)))^(-1) (x-p(s)). Thus mu, R_s and r_s are these actual laws; the tilts mean normalized exponential reweighting of the stated base measures. Let gamma be the canonical centered variance-one Gaussian on E.\nFor every s in S, r_s is a probability measure, r_s is absolutely continuous with respect to gamma, the canonical ENNReal relative entropy D_KL(r_s || gamma) is not infinity, and grad rho_s belongs to L^2(r_s). With finiteness established, the real conversion of that same relative entropy satisfies\n    (D_KL(r_s || gamma)).toReal <= eta(s)^2 d / 2.\nThe gradient is the real inner-product Riesz representative of the Frechet derivative; the Hessian in the assumptions is the evaluated second Frechet derivative. The result asserts L^2 membership of the actual residual gradient and does not assert pointwise differentiability of a chosen log Radon-Nikodym representative.",
    "text_sha256": "0579905f7b98f1c90e6d90ef98a07469df03153e902488c94577a3b640e57a14",
    "decoder": "Independent packet-only mathematical decoder. Inherited generic ASTIS project instructions, memory summary, skill catalog and environment context were visible, including generic project/source names. No packet-specific original source text, title, theorem anchor, proof, source identity, semantic review, repair, project mathematical files or compiler was accessed. This records the limited packet-only input boundary and does not claim completely context-free fresh source blindness.",
