      "anchor": "SPHMC arXiv2609.06906v1 S2 normalized hypotheses/prox/RGO/KL; S4.Ex8 standardized posterior, FIRST S4.E6/S4.SS1.p4.3 numerical KL/Fisher ingredient.",
      "wording_status": "faithful paraphrase",
      "attribution": "Authored omitted numerical canonical-KL integration ingredient from the source GaussianLSI/Fisher/moment mechanism. The paper does not print this standalone existential-witness join. Exact1357 StatementSeal and independently reconstructed exhaustive source graph admitted before proof; original citation and locator rejections and separately reviewed minimal overlays retained. This is not T2, W2 or full FIRST4.6."
    },
    "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional complete real Hilbert space with its Borel structure, including rank zero, and S a measurable parameter space. Let V be globally C2 with kappa>=1 and kappa^-1 norm(v)^2<=D²V(x)[v,v]<=norm(v)^2 for every x,v. For measurable eta/y with every eta(s)>0, there exists a measurable unique stationary proximal point p. Define the actual normalized volume tilt mu, its actual quadratic RGO reweighting R, its actual affine standardization r about that same p, the displayed smooth residual rho, and gamma=stdGaussian E. For every s, r(s) is a probability, absolutely continuous with respect to gamma, canonical KL is finite, gradient rho(s) is L2(r(s)), and canonical KL(r(s)||gamma).toReal<=eta(s)^2*real(finrank E)/2. No step-size upper bound, caller witness, law, coherence, domain or desired-bound certificate is assumed.",
    "formulae": [
      {
        "label": "Numerical canonical KL bound for the actual standardized RGO",
        "tex": "D_{\\mathrm{KL}}(r_s\\Vert\\gamma)\\le\\frac{\\eta_s^2 d}{2},\\qquad d=\\dim_{\\mathbb R}E,\\quad\\gamma=\\mathrm{stdGaussian}(E)."
      }
